{"update passes nil into save_host when host id no longer exists, causing host.host = ... on nil and a 500 error instead of handling stale records": 0.9031753540039062, "Legacy setting values are inserted exactly as stored (with schemes or paths like http://discourse.org), but new lookup only compares URI(referer).host, so migrated hosts stop matching": 0.9833975434303284, "Migration query can return no rows when embed_category override was never saved, causing nil indexing before uncategorized fallback runs, which can abort normal upgrades": 0.9200473427772522, "Validator accepts hosts with ports, but lookup drops the request port by using uri.host only, so hosts like example.com:3000 never match incoming referers": 0.9621596336364746, "Removing configured-host check from expandable_first_post? means deleted embeddable host records no longer disable the expandable embedded-first-post UI when embed_truncate is enabled": 0.5024721622467041, "The _ids branch always replaces the id array and deletes the original field, so when side-loaded records are missing, it creates entries from failed lookups and loses original ids": 0.9139724373817444}